{"id":"mahabharata-4-064","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":64,"title":"चतुःषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 64 · Uttara gives the credit to a god's son","summary":{"en":"Uttara enters, sees Kanka bleeding, and makes his father beg Kanka's pardon. Asked about his victory, he says that it was not he but a god's son who routed the Kurus and recovered the cattle, and that the hero would reveal himself in a few days.","kn":"ಒಳಬಂದ ಉತ್ತರನು ಕಂಕನಿಗೆ ರಕ್ತ ಸುರಿಯುತ್ತಿರುವುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ತಂದೆಯಿಂದ ಕಂಕನ ಕ್ಷಮೆ ಕೇಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿಜಯದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ, ಕುರುಗಳನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸಿ ಗೋವುಗಳನ್ನು ಮರಳಿಸಿದವನು ತಾನಲ್ಲ, ಒಬ್ಬ ದೇವಪುತ್ರ, ಕೆಲವು ದಿನಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಆ ವೀರನು ತನ್ನನ್ನು ತೋರಿಸಿಕೊಳ್ಳುವನು ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"उत्तर भीतर आकर कङ्क को रक्तरंजित देखता है और पिता से कङ्क की क्षमा माँगवाता है। अपनी विजय के बारे में पूछे जाने पर वह कहता है कि कुरुओं को भगाने और गौएँ लौटाने वाला वह नहीं, एक देवपुत्र था, और वह वीर कुछ दिनों में स्वयं को प्रकट करेगा।","te":"లోపలికి వచ్చిన ఉత్తరుడు కంకుడు రక్తం కారుతుండడం చూసి తండ్రి చేత కంకుని క్షమాపణ అడిగిస్తాడు. విజయం గురించి అడగగా, కురువులను ఓడించి గోవులను తిరిగి తెచ్చినది తాను కాదని, ఒక దేవపుత్రుడని, కొద్ది రోజుల్లో ఆ వీరుడు తనను తాను వెల్లడిస్తాడని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"உள்ளே வந்த உத்தரன் கங்கனுக்கு இரத்தம் வழிவதைக் கண்டு தந்தையைக் கங்கனிடம் மன்னிப்புக் கேட்கச் செய்கிறான். வெற்றி பற்றிக் கேட்டதும், குருக்களை விரட்டிப் பசுக்களை மீட்டது தானல்ல, ஒரு தேவ மைந்தன், சில நாட்களில் அவ்வீரன் தன்னை வெளிப்படுத்துவான் என்கிறான்.","ml":"ഉത്തരൻ അകത്തുവന്ന് രക്തം വാർന്ന് നിൽക്കുന്ന കങ്കനെ കാണുന്നു; പിതാവിനെക്കൊണ്ട് കങ്കനോട് മാപ്പ് ചോദിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. വിജയത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ചോദിച്ചപ്പോൾ, കുരുക്കളെ തോൽപ്പിച്ച് പശുക്കളെ വീണ്ടെടുത്തത് താനല്ലെന്നും ഒരു ദേവപുത്രനാണെന്നും, ആ വീരൻ കുറച്ചു ദിവസങ്ങൾക്കകം സ്വയം വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.64; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"वैवाहिकपर्व","titleEn":"Vaivahika Parva (The wedding)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो राज्ञः सुतो ज्येष्ठः प्राविशत्पृथिवींजयः ।\nसोऽभिवाद्य पितुः पादौ धर्मराजमपश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king's eldest son, the conqueror of the earth, entered, bowed at his father's feet, and saw Yudhishthira."}},{"n":2,"text":"स तं रुधिरसंसिक्तमनेकाग्रमनागसम् ।\nभूमावासीनमेकान्ते सैरन्ध्र्या समुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw him sprinkled with blood, distracted, though blameless, sitting alone on the ground, with Sairandhri attending him."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः पप्रच्छ पितरं त्वरमाण इवोत्तरः ।\nकेनायं ताडितो राजन्केन पापमिदं कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Uttara, in haste, asked his father, \"Who struck him, O king? Who did this wrong?\""}},{"text":"विराट उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Virata said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"मयायं ताडितो जिह्मो न चाप्येतावदर्हति ।\nप्रशस्यमाने यः शूरे त्वयि षण्ढं प्रशंसति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I struck this crooked man; he did not even deserve this much, for when you are being praised as a hero he praises a eunuch.\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"अकार्यं ते कृतं राजन्क्षिप्रमेव प्रसाद्यताम् ।\nमा त्वा ब्रह्मविषं घोरं समूलमपि निर्दहेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You have done what should not be done, O king. Quickly appease him, lest the terrible poison of a brahmin burn you up, root and all.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"स पुत्रस्य वचः श्रुत्वा विराटो राष्ट्रवर्धनः ।\nक्षमयामास कौन्तेयं भस्मच्छन्नमिवानलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his son's words, Virata, who made his realm prosper, begged pardon of Kunti's son, who was like a fire hidden in ashes."}},{"n":7,"text":"क्षमयन्तं तु राजानं पाण्डवः प्रत्यभाषत ।\nचिरं क्षान्तमिदं राजन्न मन्युर्विद्यते मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the king begged pardon, the Pandava replied, \"I forgave this long ago, O king; I feel no anger.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"यदि ह्येतत्पतेद्भूमौ रुधिरं मम नस्ततः ।\nसराष्ट्रस्त्वं महाराज विनश्येथा न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If the blood from my nose had fallen to the ground, you with your kingdom would surely have perished, great king.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"न दूषयामि ते राजन्यच्च हन्याददूषकम् ।\nबलवन्तं महाराज क्षिप्रं दारुणमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I do not blame you, O king, but when one strikes a blameless, strong man, swift and terrible harm comes.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"शोणिते तु व्यतिक्रान्ते प्रविवेश बृहन्नडा ।\nअभिवाद्य विराटं च कङ्कं चाप्युपतिष्ठत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the bleeding had stopped, Brihannada came in, saluted Virata, and stood by Kanka."}},{"n":11,"text":"क्षमयित्वा तु कौरव्यं रणादुत्तरमागतम् ।\nप्रशशंस ततो मत्स्यः शृण्वतः सव्यसाचिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having appeased the Kuru for the king, the Matsya, with Uttara returned from battle, praised him in the hearing of Savyasachin."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वया दायादवानस्मि कैकेयीनन्दिवर्धन ।\nत्वया मे सदृशः पुत्रो न भूतो न भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Through you, joy of Kaikeyi, I have a worthy heir. There has been and will be no son like you.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"पदं पदसहस्रेण यश्चरन्नापराध्नुयात् ।\nतेन कर्णेन ते तात कथमासीत्समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My son, how did you meet Karna, who in a thousand steps never errs?\""}},{"n":14,"text":"मनुष्यलोके सकले यस्य तुल्यो न विद्यते ।\nयः समुद्र इवाक्षोभ्यः कालाग्निरिव दुःसहः ।\nतेन भीष्मेण ते तात कथमासीत्समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How did you meet Bhishma, my son, who has no equal in the whole world of men, unshakable as the ocean, unbearable as the fire of time?\""}},{"n":15,"text":"आचार्यो वृष्णिवीराणां पाण्डवानां च यो द्विजः ।\nसर्वक्षत्रस्य चाचार्यः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nतेन द्रोणेन ते तात कथमासीत्समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How did you meet Drona, my son, the teacher of the Vrishni heroes and the Pandavas, the brahmin teacher of all kshatriyas, best of all who bear weapons?\""}},{"n":16,"text":"आचार्यपुत्रो यः शूरः सर्वशस्त्रभृतामपि ।\nअश्वत्थामेति विख्यातः कथं तेन समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How did you meet the teacher's son, the hero known as Ashvatthama, foremost of all weapon-bearers?\""}},{"n":17,"text":"रणे यं प्रेक्ष्य सीदन्ति हृतस्वा वणिजो यथा ।\nकृपेण तेन ते तात कथमासीत्समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How did you meet Kripa, my son, at the sight of whom men in battle sink like ruined merchants?\""}},{"n":18,"text":"पर्वतं योऽभिविध्येत राजपुत्रो महेषुभिः ।\nदुर्योधनेन ते तात कथमासीत्समागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How did you meet Duryodhana, the prince who could pierce a mountain with his great arrows?\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"न मया निर्जिता गावो न मया निर्जिताः परे ।\nकृतं तु कर्म तत्सर्वं देवपुत्रेण केनचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I did not win the cattle, nor did I defeat the enemy. All that was done by some son of a god.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"स हि भीतं द्रवन्तं मां देवपुत्रो न्यवारयत् ।\nस चातिष्ठद्रथोपस्थे वज्रहस्तनिभो युवा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That son of a god stopped me as I fled in terror, and stood on the chariot's seat, a young man like Indra with the thunderbolt in hand.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तेन ता निर्जिता गावस्तेन ते कुरवो जिताः ।\nतस्य तत्कर्म वीरस्य न मया तात तत्कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He won back the cattle and he defeated the Kurus. That was that hero's deed, father, not mine.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"स हि शारद्वतं द्रोणं द्रोणपुत्रं च वीर्यवान् ।\nसूतपुत्रं च भीष्मं च चकार विमुखाञ्शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That mighty one turned Kripa, Drona, Drona's son, Karna and Bhishma away with arrows.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"दुर्योधनं च समरे सनागमिव यूथपम् ।\nप्रभग्नमब्रवीद्भीतं राजपुत्रं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He spoke to the fleeing, frightened prince Duryodhana, mighty in battle, like a lead elephant with its herd.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"न हास्तिनपुरे त्राणं तव पश्यामि किंचन ।\nव्यायामेन परीप्सस्व जीवितं कौरवात्मज ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I see no refuge for you in Hastinapura. Save your life by effort, son of the Kauravas.'\""}},{"n":25,"text":"न मोक्ष्यसे पलायंस्त्वं राजन्युद्धे मनः कुरु ।\nपृथिवीं भोक्ष्यसे जित्वा हतो वा स्वर्गमाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You will not escape by running, O king. Set your mind to fight. By victory you will enjoy the earth, or if slain you will reach heaven.'\""}},{"n":26,"text":"स निवृत्तो नरव्याघ्रो मुञ्चन्वज्रनिभाञ्शरान् ।\nसचिवैः संवृतो राजा रथे नाग इव श्वसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That tiger among men turned back, loosing arrows like thunderbolts, the king surrounded by his counselors, hissing like a serpent in his chariot.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्र मे रोमहर्षोऽभूदूरुस्तम्भश्च मारिष ।\nयदभ्रघनसंकाशमनीकं व्यधमच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My hair stood on end and my thighs stiffened, sir, when he scattered with arrows that army that looked like a mass of clouds.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"तत्प्रणुद्य रथानीकं सिंहसंहननो युवा ।\nकुरूंस्तान्प्रहसन्राजन्वासांस्यपहरद्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Breaking that chariot force, that young man with a lion's build, laughing, mighty, took away the Kurus' clothes.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एकेन तेन वीरेण षड्रथाः परिवारिताः ।\nशार्दूलेनेव मत्तेन मृगास्तृणचरा वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That one hero surrounded six chariot-warriors, like a maddened tiger among grass-eating deer in the forest.\""}},{"text":"विराट उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Virata said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"क्व स वीरो महाबाहुर्देवपुत्रो महायशाः ।\nयो मे धनमवाजैषीत्कुरुभिर्ग्रस्तमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where is that mighty-armed hero, the famed son of a god, who won my wealth back from the Kurus' grasp in battle?\""}},{"n":31,"text":"इच्छामि तमहं द्रष्टुमर्चितुं च महाबलम् ।\nयेन मे त्वं च गावश्च रक्षिता देवसूनुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I wish to see and honor that mighty one, the son of a god, by whom you and the cattle were saved.\""}},{"text":"उत्तर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Uttara said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"अन्तर्धानं गतस्तात देवपुत्रः प्रतापवान् ।\nस तु श्वो वा परश्वो वा मन्ये प्रादुर्भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The glorious son of a god has vanished, father. I think he will appear tomorrow or the day after.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"एवमाख्यायमानं तु छन्नं सत्रेण पाण्डवम् ।\nवसन्तं तत्र नाज्ञासीद्विराटः पार्थमर्जुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though told this, Virata did not recognize Partha Arjuna, the Pandava who lived there hidden in disguise."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततः पार्थोऽभ्यनुज्ञातो विराटेन महात्मना ।\nप्रददौ तानि वासांसि विराटदुहितुः स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with the great-souled Virata's leave, Partha himself gave those garments to Virata's daughter."}},{"n":35,"text":"उत्तरा तु महार्हाणि विविधानि तनूनि च ।\nप्रतिगृह्याभवत्प्रीता तानि वासांसि भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Uttara, the lovely princess, was delighted to receive those varied precious, fine garments."}},{"n":36,"text":"मन्त्रयित्वा तु कौन्तेय उत्तरेण रहस्तदा ।\nइतिकर्तव्यतां सर्वां राजन्यथ युधिष्ठिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kunti's son consulted Uttara in private about all that should be done regarding Yudhishthira."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततस्तथा तद्व्यदधाद्यथावत्पुरुषर्षभ ।\nसह पुत्रेण मत्स्यस्य प्रहृष्टो भरतर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And then that best of men, the delighted bull of the Bharatas, together with the Matsya king's son, arranged all as required."}}]}]}